  "question": {
    "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi></math> is the time period of simple pendulum on the earth&#39;s surface. Its time period becomes <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mi>T</mi></math> when taken to a height <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> (equal to earth&#39;s radius) above the earth&#39;s surface. Then, the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> will be:",
